{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_65","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('arena.js');s=p.read_text();s='\\\\n'.join(line for line in s.split('\\\\n') if not line.startswith('  async capture()'));p.write_text(s)\np=Path('main.js');s=p.read_text();s=s.replace(\\\"const touch=controls.last==='touch'&&screen\"'!=='\"'attract'&&\"'!modal&&!hubEnded;$('\"'touch-action').hidden=\"'!touch;\", \"const touch=controls.last==='\"'touch'&&screen\"'!=='\"'attract'&&\"'!modal&&!hubEnded;const nearRival=game.players.some(q=>!q.goalie&&q.team!==p.team&&Math.hypot(q.x-p.x,q.z-p.z)<2.8);$('\"'touch-action').hidden=\"'!touch||(game.puck.owner!==p.i&&!nearRival);\")\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('\"'test.py');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"  check('touch layout detected'\\\", \\\"  phone.evaluate('__PUCK__.game.givePuck(__PUCK__.game.seats[0].index)')\\\\n  phone.wait_for_timeout(150)\\\\n  check('touch layout detected'\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"  for tab in ['testing','engine','prompt']:\\\",\\\"  for tab in ['testing','engine','prompt']:\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"   page.evaluate(\\\\\\\"__PUCK__.action('resume')\\\\\\\")\\\", \\\"   page.locator('[data-credit=\\\\\\\"licenses\\\\\\\"]').click()\\\\n   check('embedded third-party license notices','The MIT License' in page.locator('#credit-text').inner_text() and 'Apache License' in page.locator('#credit-text').inner_text())\\\\n   page.evaluate(\\\\\\\"__PUCK__.action('resume')\\\\\\\")\\\")\np.write_text(s)\nPY\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('../exit-interview.json');m=json.loads(p.read_text())\nm['sourceInformation']['tech']='Three.js r180 (0.180.0), WebGPURenderer with WebGPU by default and WebGL 2 compatibility fallback; Rapier 0.19.3; Gamepad API; Web Audio API; AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client 1.4.0; esbuild 0.28.2 build tool. All runtime dependencies, WASM and fonts embedded.'\nm['sourceInformation']['testing']='Headless testing as authorized: deterministic Rapier checks and full AI match, Chromium 153 WebGPU, emulated standard gamepads for 1–4 seats, two keyboards, Pixel 7 touch gestures, Web Audio analyser, file:// boot, four official AI Hub scenarios including 150 ms latency / 50 ms jitter / 5% loss. Visual screenshots use WebGL compatibility because software WebGPU capture is unreliable. Physical controller, real mobile hardware and subjective listening quality: unknown.'\nm['sourceInformation']['research']='none; no internet search or source research. Downloaded only dependencies and the explicitly requested AI Hub contract, client and harness.'\nm['testingFeedback']=[\n '3 confirmed game issues caught by gameplay tests and visual review: AI failed to convert shots into goals, rink advertising was occluded, and foreground light rigs obstructed the rink. All corrected. Test-only selector and wall-clock timing errors were corrected separately.',\n '0 confirmed critical or game-breaking game issues. Physical controller feel, real phone behavior and subjective sound quality are unknown.',\n 'The deterministic full AI match exposed scoreless AI play. The official AI Hub harness also verified normal two-player play, stressed four-player play, host departure and dedicated-server hosting.',\n 'Raw pixel capture from headless software WebGPU was least helpful: frames could be blank and readback failed. Gameplay was checked from state, while isolated WebGL compatibility screenshots verified appearance.'\n]\nm['engineFeedback']=[\n 'Three.js node materials and AnimationMixer made it possible to build an entirely procedural ink-styled rink with animated skaters and no asset downloads at runtime.',\n 'Software WebGPU screenshots/readback were unreliable in this environment. Long WebGL interaction tests were also slow, so visual capture was separated from state tests and input checks used simulation-aware waits.',\n 'The hockey simulation: possession, team AI, checking, passing, goalies, match flow, input routing and the authoritative shared-world network layer.',\n 'Coordinating fixed-step Rapier physics, Three.js animation, WebGPU presentation, controller focus and delayed network input without losing brief button actions.',\n 'none; the engines and AI Hub client are unmodified. Custom materials, gameplay and compatibility options are application code.',\n 'A first-class cel-shading material for WebGPU with straightforward ink outlines would reduce custom material work.'\n]\nm['promptFeedback']=[\n 'The specific source, procedural audio, cel/ink art direction and controller-first constraints gave the demo a clear identity while leaving room for original arcade mechanics.',\n 'The terse source label and whether standalone multiplayer required internet play outside AI Hub were ambiguous. This demo provides standalone couch multiplayer and online shared-world play through AI Hub.',\n 'Making a complete hockey match, six-drill tutorial, multi-device controls, dev tools and resilient multiplayer fit together in one self-contained HTML.',\n 'Provide the Hub contract locally and specify whether standalone multiplayer must include internet play in addition to couch play.'\n]\np.write_text(json.dumps(m,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\nnpm run --silent build && PUCK_VISUAL=1 npm run --silent test\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
